**Given:**

Length of rectangular garden (l) = 20 m

Breadth of rectangular garden (b) = 8 m

**Formula Used:**

Area of a rectangle = length × breadth

Area of a square = side × side = s²

Diagonal of a square = ssqrt{2}

**Calculation:**

Areaᵣₑ꜀ₜₐₙgₗₑ = l × b = 20 m × 8 m = 160 m²

Areaₛqᵤₐᵣₑ = 160 m²

Side (s) of the square garden:

s² = 160

s = sqrt{160}

s = sqrt{16 times 10}

s = 4sqrt{10} m

Length of the diagonal of the square garden:

Diagonal = ssqrt{2}

Diagonal = (4sqrt{10}) × sqrt{2}

Diagonal = 4sqrt{10 times 2}

Diagonal = 4sqrt{20}

Diagonal = 4sqrt{4 times 5}

Diagonal = 4 × 2sqrt{5}

Diagonal = 8sqrt{5} m

**∴ The length of the diagonal of the square garden is 8sqrt{5} m.**
